# XSH sigismember()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.sigismember.001
anchor     functions/sigismember.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       With a set made by sigemptyset() and sigaddset(SIGUSR2),
           sigismember() returns exactly 1 for SIGUSR2 and exactly 0 for
           SIGUSR1 and SIGRTMIN; on a full set it returns 1 for SIGUSR1.
note       Where <signal.h> lacks SIGRTMIN (reported by XBD.signal.h.006),
           that one non-member is skipped with a note, so that the sets'
           own tests are not blocked by a build failure here.
test       t/001-one-or-zero.c
